1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,483
You know how shares work.

2
00:00:03,483 --> 00:00:05,013
But what is a sukuk,

3
00:00:05,013 --> 00:00:06,961
on the Pakistan Stock Exchange?

4
00:00:09,711 --> 00:00:11,342
Start with something real.

5
00:00:11,342 --> 00:00:13,285
Say, a stretch of motorway.

6
00:00:14,735 --> 00:00:16,265
A sukuk is a certificate

7
00:00:16,265 --> 00:00:17,795
that gives you a share

8
00:00:17,795 --> 00:00:19,637
in owning an asset like this.

9
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:23,365
Every certificate has the same value,

10
00:00:23,365 --> 00:00:25,542
so each one is an equal slice.

11
00:00:27,392 --> 00:00:30,140
In Pakistan, government sukuk have used

12
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,112
assets like the M-1 motorway

13
00:00:32,112 --> 00:00:34,687
and Jinnah International Airport.

14
00:00:37,937 --> 00:00:39,167
Here's how it works.

15
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:40,394
Investors pay money,

16
00:00:40,394 --> 00:00:42,176
and the government sells them

17
00:00:42,176 --> 00:00:43,717
a share of the asset.

18
00:00:47,627 --> 00:00:49,958
But the government still needs the motorway,

19
00:00:49,958 --> 00:00:51,488
so it leases it back.

20
00:00:52,896 --> 00:00:54,588
For using it, the government

21
00:00:54,588 --> 00:00:56,711
pays rent to the sukuk holders.

22
00:00:57,761 --> 00:00:59,041
That's the big idea.

23
00:00:59,041 --> 00:01:01,218
Your return is rent from an asset,

24
00:01:01,218 --> 00:01:02,941
not interest on a loan.

25
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:08,204
That's why it's called an Ijarah sukuk.

26
00:01:08,204 --> 00:01:09,630
Ijarah means lease.

27
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:14,013
When the term ends,

28
00:01:14,013 --> 00:01:16,350
after one, three, five or ten years,

29
00:01:16,350 --> 00:01:18,872
the government buys the asset back,

30
00:01:19,222 --> 00:01:21,380
and investors get their money back.

31
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:25,160
So where does

32
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:26,690
the stock exchange come in?

33
00:01:28,126 --> 00:01:29,731
Since December 2023,

34
00:01:29,731 --> 00:01:32,540
Government of Pakistan Ijarah Sukuk

35
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:35,358
have been auctioned through PSX.

36
00:01:36,988 --> 00:01:39,413
They come in units of 5,000 rupees,

37
00:01:39,413 --> 00:01:42,089
small enough for a retail investor.

38
00:01:43,639 --> 00:01:45,254
Open a brokerage account

39
00:01:45,254 --> 00:01:46,735
and a CDC sub-account,

40
00:01:46,735 --> 00:01:48,865
and you can buy and sell them

41
00:01:48,865 --> 00:01:49,745
like shares.

42
00:01:51,495 --> 00:01:53,071
By September 2024,

43
00:01:53,071 --> 00:01:55,610
these PSX auctions had raised

44
00:01:55,610 --> 00:01:58,049
over one trillion rupees.

45
00:01:59,499 --> 00:02:00,751
One thing to watch:

46
00:02:00,751 --> 00:02:02,134
sell before maturity,

47
00:02:02,134 --> 00:02:03,964
and the price may be higher

48
00:02:03,964 --> 00:02:05,678
or lower than you paid.

49
00:02:07,728 --> 00:02:09,258
So a sukuk is simple.

50
00:02:09,258 --> 00:02:11,688
You own a slice of a real asset,

51
00:02:11,688 --> 00:02:13,218
and it pays you rent.
